<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-aesculapii-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Danio aesculapii cellular Turing wavenumber at 21 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 86.4/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2, supersedes the pass-1 audit. Anisotropic Schnakenberg system at λ_c = 2.08e-05 m (nominal 21 µm, log10 = -4.682), Holocene 0 Ma, chronoseries 1/5, successor D. albolineatus. Trace -0.5044, det 1.2544, R=28 above R_c=1.6725, equal-diffusion and successor (R=1.20) controls have negative diffusion-weighted trace and σ(k_c)<0. Dorsal field selects vertical bars at 16 px = 20.8 µm; ventral field breaks them into spots. Linear-regime Pearson r of log|û(k_c)| vs t is >0.999 with log-RMSE 0.025. Specimen body circularity 0.262 (reference circle 1), aspect 4.18, KS luminance 0.147. GIF 12 frames, 1437×480, cv_sim_similarity 93.2 against the CC BY-SA photograph. Formula k_c exceeds argmax σ by 0.0785 rad/px, now a measurement, and --self-test opens the GIF (12 frames, 1437×480, cv >= 58). Pass-1 R1 and R2 are closed. Weighted overall 86.4. Overall 86.4/100 (faithfulness 84.7, reproducibility 90.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit cfb8887378258c806d4412f6b1faac9a96299054; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 84, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 88, Reproducibility package 92. Output judged: docs/media/danio_aesculapii_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-danio-aesculapii-turing-wavelength-s0.py at cfb8887378258c806d4412f6b1faac9a96299054, image/png, 473586 B, 1632×912 px, artifact_sha256 7830914d2b5b6fb1b31835e5cda4b4ca15daef5474de1cb31f0018f66877ba62 (sha256 7830914d2b5b6fb1b31835e5cda4b4ca15daef5474de1cb31f0018f66877ba62), spec_fingerprint 243520b4201453b66768f25b30961995e65983baa128d9b7d5af4520fe5a690c. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 243520b4201453b66768f25b30961995e65983baa128d9b7d5af4520fe5a690c; artifact_sha256: 7830914d2b5b6fb1b31835e5cda4b4ca15daef5474de1cb31f0018f66877ba62; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/danio_aesculapii_turing_wavelength_s0/danio_aesculapii_parichy2015_plate.jpg=26511cee521d38a6..., datasets/danio_aesculapii_turing_wavelength_s0/danio_aesculapii_specimen.png=6c6f62863f3ec000...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-danio-aesculapii-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 critical-wavenumber formula and dispersion relation | Nakamasu 2009 and Yamanaka & Kondo 2014 melanophore-xanthophore contact interactions | Kullander & Fang 2009 vertical bars; Spiewak et al. 2018 endothelin-linked Danio pattern diversification; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg A=0.14, B=0.98, R=28 chosen so λ_c = 2.08e-05 m | Dorsal anisotropy versus ventral isotropy as the vertical-bar transition | Successor inhibitor collapse to R=1.20 at the same activator diffusivity; transfer_boundary: The whole-animal GIF maps the 249.6 µm cellular field onto the photographed silhouette so orientation can be scored. It is not a claim that adult bars are 20.8 µm apart.; does_not_claim: That a paper measured 21.0 µm on D. aesculapii | That the render is a pixel copy of the photograph | Parameters copied from the 1.009 mm organ-scale sibling." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.64e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-aesculapii-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Danio aesculapii cellular Turing wavenumber at 21 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — Parameter expressivity: 84/100" ;
