<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-danio-aesculapii-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Danio aesculapii cellular Turing wavenumber at 21 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) (Danio aesculapii)",
        "Danio aesculapii cellular Turing wavenumber at 21 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) faithfully reproduces Danio aesculapii morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-danio-aesculapii-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-danio-aesculapii-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-danio-aesculapii-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-danio-aesculapii-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Danio aesculapii specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-danio-aesculapii-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Danio aesculapii" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Parameters copied from the 1.009 mm organ-scale sibling",
        "does_not_claim: That a paper measured 21.0 µm on D. aesculapii",
        "does_not_claim: That the render is a pixel copy of the photograph",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Dorsal anisotropy versus ventral isotropy as the vertical-bar transition",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg A=0.14, B=0.98, R=28 chosen so λ_c = 2.08e-05 m",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Successor inhibitor collapse to R=1.20 at the same activator diffusivity",
        "reported_in_source: Kullander & Fang 2009 vertical bars; Spiewak et al. 2018 endothelin-linked Danio pattern diversification",
        "reported_in_source: Nakamasu 2009 and Yamanaka & Kondo 2014 melanophore-xanthophore contact interactions",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 critical-wavenumber formula and dispersion relation",
        "transfer_boundary: The whole-animal GIF maps the 249.6 µm cellular field onto the photographed silhouette so orientation can be scored. It is not a claim that adult bars are 20.8 µm apart." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Danio aesculapii (Holocene (Extant))" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Pisces (Ichthyes)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Danio" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-danio-aesculapii-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/danio_aesculapii_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Danio aesculapii; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952 critical-wavenumber formula and dispersion relation | Nakamasu 2009 and Yamanaka & Kondo 2014 melanophore-xanthophore contact interactions | Kullander & Fang 2009 vertical bars; Spiewak et al. 2018 endothelin-linked Danio pattern diversification; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg A=0.14, B=0.98, R=28 chosen so λ_c = 2.08e-05 m | Dorsal anisotropy versus ventral isotropy as the vertical-bar transition | Successor inhibitor collapse to R=1.20 at the same activator diffusivity; transfer_boundary: The whole-animal GIF maps the 249.6 µm cellular field onto the photographed silhouette so orientation can be scored. It is not a claim that adult bars are 20.8 µm apart.; does_not_claim: That a paper measured 21.0 µm on D. aesculapii | That the render is a pixel copy of the photograph | Parameters copied from the 1.009 mm organ-scale sibling]; phenomenon_size: 20 µm (2.018e-05 m, log10=-4.695 m, tier=4_cellular_10um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 20 µm to 4.5 cm): 20 µm:danio-aesculapii-bioelectric-polarity, 63 µm:danio-aesculapii-vertex-packing, 1.0 mm:danio-aesculapii-turing-wavelength, 2.0 mm:danio-aesculapii-clock-wavefront, 4.5 mm:danio-aesculapii-morphogen-condensation, 5.5 mm:danio-aesculapii-elastic-buckling, 6.3 mm:danio-aesculapii-flux-canalization, 8.8 mm:danio-aesculapii-branching-tree" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0808622106>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1315416111>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
